{"nodes": [{"id": "supabase_tests_config_schema_test_config_schema_test", "label": "config_schema_test (card ^ref-10)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "supabase/tests/config_schema_test.sql", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Turns ^ref-10's one-time reading into an assertion run on every apply: the six config tables exist; the four rate-bearing ones (smoke_fee_tiers, config_settings, product_prices, packaging_full_stock) carry effective_from, created_by and created_at; no mutable rate column exists anywhere. The last block deliberately asserts that packaging_full_stock's unique key is still BROKEN \u2014 (packaging_item_id, location_id, effective_from) with a nullable location_id stores two GLOBAL rows for one date because Postgres treats NULLs as distinct \u2014 so the day someone fixes the index the assert fails and points at fn_set_packaging_full_stock's application-code guard as now-dead code."}], "edges": [{"source": "supabase_tests_config_schema_test_config_schema_test", "target": "supabase_migrations_20260908000002_identity_config_config_settings", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "supabase/tests/config_schema_test.sql", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "supabase_tests_config_schema_test_config_schema_test", "target": "supabase_migrations_20260908000002_identity_config_smoke_fee_tiers", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "supabase/tests/config_schema_test.sql", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "supabase_tests_config_schema_test_config_schema_test", "target": "supabase_migrations_20260908000004_stock_and_branch_daily_products", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "supabase/tests/config_schema_test.sql", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "supabase